  "summary_en": "European Parliament STOA briefing outlining legal and ethical challenges of AI: definition, legal personhood for robots, transparency and explainability, liability, bias, and human oversight. It argues for a guiding ethical framework based on the Charter of Fundamental Rights and flexible regulatory tools such as sandboxes and sunset clauses.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "No agreed AI definition; technology-neutral definition based on autonomy and function suggested",
   "Flexible instruments (delegated acts, sunset clauses, sandboxes) address the pacing problem",
   "Robot personhood is criticised as overvaluing robot capabilities",
   "Advanced robots should have a 'black box' recording decisions; right to explanation needed",
   "Ethical framework based on Charter of Fundamental Rights should safeguard human oversight"
